{:edb/db-before-t 2046 :edb/db-after-t 2047 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535359 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:45:08.862Z" 13194139535359 true] [17592186100836 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345736 13194139535359 true] [17592186100836 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345750 13194139535359 true] [17592186100837 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345722 13194139535359 true] [17592186100837 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345729 13194139535359 true] [17592186100849 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345743 13194139535359 true] [17592186345722 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345723 13194139535359 true] [17592186345722 1089 "q-168148" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345722 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535359 true] [17592186345722 1100 "Find the general solution to the following equation. \n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,,\\,x>0\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345722 1113 #uuid "2d42bd2f-d571-53e4-a5f4-39d200878b23" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345722 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-1}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{-1}\\,.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $y(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x})+{z}^{-1} & ={x}^{2}{({z}^{-1})}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{x}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{z} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{x}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{z} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{z}{x} & =-x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}\\,z & =-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nP(x)=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-x\\,.\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\int 1/xdx} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x{|}^{-1}} \\\\  & =|x{|}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUnder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}\\,z) & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot (-x) \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}z & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{z}{x}] & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{z}{x}]\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{z}{x} & =-x+C \\\\ z & =-{x}^{2}+Cx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =-{x}^{2}+Cx \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{Cx-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345724 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345725 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345726 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345727 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345728 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1041 "selection" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345727 13194139535359 true] [17592186345723 1110 #uuid "d9a07b61-60fc-5b9b-8c45-309d59c6f207" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345724 1034 "y=\\frac{Cx}{{x}^{2}+1}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345724 1111 #uuid "b6bbbe47-a037-5eb4-b24b-aa59631a181f" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345725 1034 "y=2x-C{x}^{2}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345725 1111 #uuid "babadbc6-14ba-51f7-8d2f-fcd23cc336d9" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345726 1034 "y=\\frac{C{x}^{2}+1}{x}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345726 1111 #uuid "84d204df-5e8c-531a-a608-9ae8be1017ea" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345727 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{Cx-{x}^{2}}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345727 1111 #uuid "725e6706-ea19-59ca-8f66-25375de7ec48" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345728 1034 "y=\\frac{x+C}{{x}^{2}}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345728 1111 #uuid "f44f39ac-eb43-5520-af1a-9a41dcc2bd15" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345729 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345730 13194139535359 true] [17592186345729 1089 "q-17541" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345729 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535359 true] [17592186345729 1100 "Find the general solution to the following equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y={x}^{2}{y}^{2}\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution* $z={y}^{-1}.$" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345729 1113 #uuid "b0ae988c-ab98-550b-a424-bb115656f091" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345729 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-1}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{-1}\\,\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ with the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{z}{x}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}{x}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}z & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}z & =-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-{x}^{2},\\,Q(x)=-{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot (\\frac{dz}{dx}-{x}^{2}z) & ={e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot (-{x}^{2}) \\\\ {e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot \\frac{dz}{dx}-{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}{x}^{2}z & =-{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}/3} \\\\ \\frac{d}{dx}(z{e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}) & =-{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(z{e}^{-{x}^{3}/3})\\,\\,dx & =-\\int {x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}\\,dx \\\\ z{e}^{-{x}^{3}/3} & ={e}^{-{x}^{3}/3}+C \\\\ z & =1+C{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =1+C{e}^{{x}^{3}/3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345731 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345732 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345733 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345734 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345735 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1041 "selection" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345733 13194139535359 true] [17592186345730 1110 #uuid "a79a2096-d403-5d04-8b50-dbd100718a4d" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345731 1034 "y={e}^{{x}^{2}}+C" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345731 1111 #uuid "82bc4b34-5844-58cc-994d-98a20bcce61c" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345732 1034 "y={(2+Cx)}^{2}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345732 1111 #uuid "cf2c3af7-5a1a-5c58-95d2-144e355f3300" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345733 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345733 1111 #uuid "f1698cf9-259c-5688-9ff1-d72970d1ba43" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345734 1034 "y={(1+\\frac{C}{{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}})}^{2}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345734 1111 #uuid "96277d50-fafa-5180-9450-1c11d3b16009" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345735 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{{x}^{3}}}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345735 1111 #uuid "5a50e1ab-8814-5cf3-8ac0-3033b21cb78e" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345736 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345737 13194139535359 true] [17592186345736 1089 "q-17558" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345736 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535359 true] [17592186345736 1100 "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{x},\\,y(1)=1,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation*\n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-3x\n$$\n\n*using the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345736 1113 #uuid "a58498f7-0f5c-5c4d-91a7-8c4aea186d9f" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345736 1145 "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-3x.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\\,.\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-3x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-3x) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{dz}{dx}+z & =-3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{d}{dx}(xz) & =-3{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(xz)\\,dx & =-\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\ xz & =-{x}^{3}+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-{x}^{3}}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{C-{x}^{3}}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{C-{x}^{3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now determine $C$ from the initial condition $y(1)=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{C-1}\\,⟹\\,C=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{2-{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345738 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345739 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345740 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345741 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345742 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1041 "selection" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345741 13194139535359 true] [17592186345737 1110 #uuid "5757c845-3b8b-50d5-9989-ee1719ab6d74" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345738 1034 "y=\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{3}}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345738 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345738 1111 #uuid "4c18d3d2-25f4-57e9-b12c-25690a55d2de" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345739 1034 "y=\\frac{-2x}{1-3{x}^{3}}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345739 1111 #uuid "bcc55cd1-c091-55b3-af32-e9c4c3a44be8" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345740 1034 "y=\\frac{2x}{1+x}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345740 1111 #uuid "23c1d6bd-a1fa-52aa-8a4b-13c1fe8ad142" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345741 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{2-{x}^{3}}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345741 1111 #uuid "923ad05e-7ac8-5daf-b97a-f1dc5cf49d7c" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345742 1034 "y={x}^{2/3}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345742 1111 #uuid "4effd12f-9ca0-553d-ab54-62a69b1f50e0" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345743 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345744 13194139535359 true] [17592186345743 1089 "q-79781" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345743 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535359 true] [17592186345743 1100 "The substitution $z={y}^{-2}$ can be used to transform the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y(1-x{y}^{2})\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345743 1113 #uuid "d4252974-7b7b-52aa-9a22-e2abec75619b" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345743 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-2{y}^{-3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{-3/2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{-3/2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{z}^{-1/2}(1-x{z}^{-1}) \\\\ {z}^{-3/2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}{z}^{-1/2}(x{z}^{-1}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now write the above equation in standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x).\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}z(x{z}^{-1}-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{2}z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}z & ={x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)={x}^{3}.$" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345745 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345746 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345747 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345748 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345749 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1041 "selection" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345746 13194139535359 true] [17592186345744 1110 #uuid "eb003d36-84f9-50eb-bf20-68dc330dd27f" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345745 1034 "\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345745 1111 #uuid "a97c1492-f94b-554c-9fa0-66c6edb3c453" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345746 1034 "{x}^{3}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345746 1111 #uuid "71c96ceb-c73c-5d1f-adde-26a520563b79" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345747 1034 "1" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345747 1111 #uuid "d5af068a-9b06-58d4-bc12-9d5dd6cd7b60" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345748 1034 "x" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345748 1111 #uuid "8526bcfc-4148-5699-a2fc-d0e4c9819ae0" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345749 1034 "{x}^{2}" 13194139535359 true] [17592186345749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535359 true] [17592186345749 1111 #uuid "23